  "body": "Issue #125 (user report): Windows waited on every other platform, and one failed package blocked the whole release.\n\n**New graph**: `windows` (new, was `release`), `linux`, `macos` start at once; `snap`, `flatpak` need `linux`; a new `publish` job (ubuntu-latest, the only job with `contents: write`) needs all five with `if: !cancelled() && startsWith(github.ref, 'refs/tags/')`, downloads every artifact that exists, builds the release page from the template (guards unchanged), adds a \"Not in this release: <platform> ... see the workflow run\" line for each build job whose result is not success, fails only if no release file at all was built, and publishes with `fail_on_unmatched_files: false`. Workflow-wide permission is `contents: read`. Triggers unchanged (vX.Y.0 tags + workflow_dispatch); a manual run builds all five and skips publish.\n\n**Validation**: YAML parses; every pwsh step parses (Windows PowerShell 5.1 parser - pwsh 7 not installed); actionlint not available; not run on GitHub. Uncertain: publish's fallback version from `cargo metadata` when the Windows job fails; download-artifact with nothing to download (continue-on-error + the asset check guard it).\n\nChangelog: none (CI only)\n\nFixes #125",
